mod 13). Squares mod 13: 0,1,4,9,3,12,10,9,3,12,10,1,4. So k² ≡ 10 (mod 13) has solutions k ≡ 6 or 7 (mod 13).\n\nLet me search for small solutions. |k| < √(39·b²) roughly. We need 39b² - 380 ≥ 0, so b² ≥ 10.\n\nLet me enumerate b from 4 upward and check if 39b² - 380 is a perfect square:\nb=4: 39·16-380 = 624-380 = 244. √244 ≈ 15.6, not perfect square.\nb=5: 39·25-380 = 975-380 = 595. No.\nb=6: 39·36-380 = 1404-380 = 1024 = 32². Yes! (k,b) = (±32, ±6).\nb=7: 39·49-380 = 1911-380 = 1531. No.\nb=8: 39·64-380 = 2496-380 = 2116 = 46². Yes! (k,b) = (±46, ±8).\nb=9: 39·81-380 = 3159-380 = 2779. No.\nb=10: 3900-380 = 3520. No.\nb=11: 4719-380 = 4339. No.\nb=12: 5616-380 = 5236. No.\nb=13: 6591-380 = 6211. No.\nb=14: 7644-380 = 7264. No.\nb=15: 8775-380 = 8395. No.\nb=16: 9984-380 = 9604 = 98². Yes! (k,b) = (±98, ±16).\nb=17: 11271-380 = 10891. √10891 ≈ 104.4. 104²=10816, 105²=11025. No.\nb=18: 12636-380 = 12256. √12256 ≈ 110.7. 110²=12100, 111²=12321. No.\nb=19: 14019-380 = 13639. No.\nb=20: 15600-380 = 15220. No.\n\nLet me check negative b too. Since the equation is k² - 39b² = -380, and b appears as b², negative b gives same k values. But then a = (20b + k)/19 changes.\n\nSo the fundamental solutions (with b > 0) are:\n(k, b) = (32, 6), (46, 8), (98, 16), ...\n\nLet me generate more using the Pell recurrence:\nFrom (k, b), next is (25k + 156b, 4k + 25b).\n\nFrom (32, 6): (25·32 + 156·6, 4·32 + 25·6) = (800 + 936, 128 + 150) = (1736, 278).\nCheck: 39·278² - 1736² = 39·77284 - 3013696 = 3014076 - 3013696 = 380. ✓\n\nFrom (46, 8): (25·46 + 156·8, 4·46 + 25·8) = (1150 + 1248, 184 + 200) = (2398, 384).\nCheck: 39·384² - 2398² = 39·147456 - 5750404 = 5750784 - 5750404 = 380. ✓\n\nFrom (98, 16): (25·98 + 156·16, 4·98 + 25·16) = (2450 + 2496, 392 + 400) = (4946, 792).\n\nNow, for each (k, b) solution, we get a = (20b + k)/19 or a = (20b - k)/19. We need a to be integer, so 19 | (20b ± k).\n\nFor (k,b) = (32, 6): \na = (120 + 32)/19 = 152/19 = 8. ✓ → (8, 6)\na = (120 - 32)/19 = 88/19. Not integer.\n\nFor (k,b) = (-32, 6):\na = (120 - 32)/19 = 88/19. No.\na = (120 + 32)/19 = 152/19 = 8. Wait, k=-32: a = (20·6 + (-32))/19 = 88/19, or a = (20·6 - (-32))/19 = 152/19 = 8. Same thing.\n\nActually, the ± k just gives both roots. So for (k,b)=(32,6), the two a values are (120+32)/19=8 and (120-32)/19=88/19 (not integer). So only a=8.\n\nFor (k,b) = (46, 8):\na = (160 + 46)/19 = 206/19. Not integer.\na = (160 - 46)/19 = 114/19 = 6. ✓ → (6, 8)\n\nFor (k,b) = (98, 16):\na = (320 + 98)/19 = 418/19 = 22. ✓ → (22, 16)\na = (320 - 98)/19 = 222/19. Not integer.\n\nFor (k,b) = (1736, 278):\na = (20·278 + 1736)/19 = (5560 + 1736)/19 = 7296/19 = 384. ✓ → (384, 278)\na = (5560 - 1736)/19 = 3824/19 = 201.26... Not integer.\n\nCheck (384, 278): a²+b² = 147456 + 77284 = 224740. 2ab-1 = 2·384·278 - 1 = 213504 - 1 = 213503. 224740/213503... 19·224740 = 4270060, 20·213503 = 4270060. ✓. a-b-1 = 384-278-1 = 105. 105 | 224740? 224740/105 = 2140.38... No! ✗.\n\nSo (384, 278) fails condition 1.\n\nFor (k,b) = (2398, 384):\na = (20·384 + 2398)/19 = (7680 + 2398)/19 = 10078/19 = 530.42... No.\na = (7680 - 2398)/19 = 5282/19 = 278. ✓ → (278, 384)\n\nCheck (278, 384): a-b-1 = 278-384-1 = -107. 107 | (278²+384²)? 278²+384² = 77284+147456 = 224740. 224740/107 = 2100.37... No. ✗.\n\nFor (k,b) = (4946, 792):\na = (20·792 + 4946)/19 = (15840 + 4946)/19 = 20786/19 = 1094. ✓ → (1094, 792)\na = (15840 - 4946)/19 = 10894/19 = 573.37... No.\n\nCheck (1094, 792): a-b-1 = 1094-792-1 = 301. a²+b² = 1094²+792² = 1196836+627264 = 1824100. 1824100/301 = 6060.13... No. ✗.\n\nHmm, so it seems like only the small solutions satisfy condition 1. Let me also check negative b values.\n\nFor b = -6, k = 32: a = (20·(-6) + 32)/19 = (-120+32)/19 = -88/19. No. a = (-120-32)/19 = -152/19 = -8. → (-8, -6).\nCheck: a-b-1 = -8-(-6)-1 = -8+6-1 = -3. -3 | 100? No. ✗.\n\nFor b = -6, k = -32: a = (-120-32)/19 = -152/19 = -8, or a = (-120+32)/19 = -88/19. Same.\n\nFor b = -8, k = 46: a = (-160+46)/19 = -114/19 = -6. → (-6, -8). a = (-160-46)/19 = -206/19. No.\nCheck (-6, -8): a-b-1 = -6+8-1 = 1. 1 | 100. ✓. And 100/95 = 20/19. ✓. Works!\n\nFor b = -8, k = -46: a = (-160-46)/19 = -206/19. No. a = (-160+46)/19 = -114/19 = -6. Same.\n\nFor b = -16, k = 98: a = (-320+98)/19 = -222/19. No. a = (-320-98)/19 = -418/19 = -22. → (-22, -16).\nCheck: a-b-1 = -22+16-1 = -7. -7 | 740? 740/7 = 105.71. No. ✗.\n\nFor b = -16, k = -98: a = (-320-98)/19 = -418/19 = -22, or a = (-320+98)/19 = -222/19. Same.\n\nFor b = -278, k = 1736: a = (-5560+1736)/19 = -3824/19. No. a = (-5560-1736)/19 = -7296/19 = -384. → (-384, -278).\nCheck: a-b-1 = -384+278-1 = -107. 107 | 224740? No. ✗.\n\nFor b = -384, k = 2398: a = (-7680+2398)/19 = -5282/19 = -278. → (-278, -384). a = (-7680-2398)/19 = -10078/19. No.\nCheck: a-b-1 = -278+384-1 = 105. 105 | 224740? No. ✗.\n\nFor b = -792, k = 4946: a = (-15840+4946)/19 = -10894/19. No. a = (-15840-4946)/19 = -20786/19 = -1094. → (-1094, -792).\nCheck: a-b-1 = -1094+792-1 = -303. 303 | 1824100? 1824100/303 = 6020.13... No. ✗.\n\nSo far, the solutions satisfying both conditions are:\n(8, 6), (-6, -8), (22, 16)\n\nWait, let me also check: are there solutions with b = -278 and the other root? We had a = -384. What about checking if there are other fundamental solutions to the Pell equation that I might have missed?\n\nLet me check more b values:\nb=21: 39·441-380 = 17199-380 = 16819. √16819 ≈ 129.7. 129²=16641, 130²=16900. No.\nb=22: 39·484-380 = 18876-380 = 18496. √18496 ≈ 136. 136² = 18496. Yes! k=136.\na = (440+136)/19 = 576/19. No. a = (440-136)/19 = 304/19 = 16. → (16, 22).\nCheck: a²+b² = 256+484 = 740. 2ab-1 = 704-1 = 703. 740/703 = 20/19? 19·740=14060, 20·703=14060. ✓. a-b-1 = 16-22-1 = -7. -7 | 740? 740/7 = 105.71. No. ✗.\n\nb = -22, k = 136: a = (-440+136)/19 = -304/19 = -16. → (-16, -22). a = (-440-136)/19 = -576/19. No.\nCheck: a-b-1 = -16+22-1 = 5. 5 | 740? 740/5 = 148. Yes! ✓. So (-16, -22) works!\n\nb = -22, k = -136: a = (-440-136)/19 = -576/19. No. a = (-440+136)/19 = -304/19 = -16. Same.\n\nSo (-16, -22) is a solution. Let me verify: a=-16, b=-22. a²+b² = 256+484 = 740. 2ab-1 = 2·352-1 = 704-1 = 703. 740/703 = 20/19 ✓. a-b-1 = -16+22-1 = 5. 5 | 740 ✓. \n\nSo we have (8,6), (-6,-8), (22,16), (-16,-22). Let me continue.\n\nb=23: 39·529-380 = 20631-380 = 20251. √20251 ≈ 142.3. 142²=20164, 143²=20449. No.\nb=24: 39·576-380 = 22464-380 = 22084. √22084 ≈ 148.6. 148²=21904, 149²=22201. No.\nb=25: 39·625-380 = 24375-380 = 23995. No.\nb=26: 39·676-380 = 26364-380 = 25984. √25984 ≈ 161.2. 161²=25921, 162²=26244. No.\nb=27: 39·729-380 = 28431-380 = 28051. No.\nb=28: 39·784-380 = 30576-380 = 30196. √30196 ≈ 173.8. 173²=29929, 174²=30276. No.\nb=29: 39·841-380 = 32799-380 = 32419. No.\nb=30: 39·900-380 = 35100-380 = 34720. No.\n\nLet me think about this more systematically. The fundamental solutions to k² - 39b² = -380 generate infinite families via Pell multiplication. But we need to find all fundamental solutions first.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The solutions I found so far with b > 0:\n(k, b) = (32, 6), (46, 8), (98, 16), (136, 22)\n\nLet me check if (136, 22) generates from any of the others via Pell. \nFrom (32, 6): next is (1736, 278). Not (136, 22).\nFrom (46, 8): next is (2398, 384). Not (136, 22).\nFrom (98, 16): next is (4946, 792). Not (136, 22).\n\nSo (136, 22) is a new fundamental solution. Let me generate its Pell descendants:\nFrom (136, 22): (25·136 + 156·22, 4·136 + 25·22) = (3400 + 3432, 544 + 550) = (6832, 1094).\na = (20·1094 + 6832)/19 = (21880 + 6832)/19 = 28712/19 = 1511.16... No.\na = (21880 - 6832)/19 = 15048/19 = 792. → (792, 1094).\nCheck: a-b-1 = 792-1094-1 = -303. 303 | (792²+1094²)? 792²=627264, 1094²=1196836, sum=1824100. 1824100/303 = 6020.13... No. ✗.\n\nb = -1094, k = 6832: a = (-21880+6832)/19 = -15048/19 = -792. → (-792, -1094).\nCheck: a-b-1 = -792+1094-1 = 301. 301 | 1824100? 1824100/301 = 6060.13... No. ✗.\n\nSo the Pell descendants don't satisfy condition 1 (at least for the ones I've checked). Let me continue searching for more fundamental solutions.\n\nb=31: 39·961-380 = 37479-380 = 37099. √37099 ≈ 192.6. 192²=36864, 193²=37249. No.\nb=32: 39·1024-380 = 39936-380 = 39556. √39556 ≈ 198.9. 198²=39204, 199²=39601. No.\nb=33: 39·1089-380 = 42471-380 = 42091. No.\nb=34: 39·1156-380 = 45084-380 = 44704. √44704 ≈ 211.4. 211²=44521, 212²=44944. No.\nb=35: 39·1225-380 = 47775-380 = 47395. No.\nb=36: 39·1296-380 = 50544-380 = 50164. √50164 ≈ 224. 224²=50176. Close but no.\nb=37: 39·1369-380 = 53391-380 = 53011. No.\nb=38: 39·1444-380 = 56316-380 = 55936. √55936 ≈ 236.5. 236²=55696, 237²=56169. No.\nb=39: 39·1521-380 = 59319-380 = 58939. No.\nb=40: 39·1600-380 = 62400-380 = 62020. No.\n\nThis is getting tedious. Let me think about whether there's a pattern or a bound.\n\nActually, let me think about condition 1 more carefully. We have a² + b² = 20(2ab-1)/19. And a - b - 1 divides a² + b².\n\nLet d = a - b - 1. Then a = b + 1 + d. \n\na² + b² = (b+1+d)² + b² = b² + 2b(1+d) + (1+d)² + b² = 2b² + 2b(1+d) + (1+d)².\n\nAnd 2ab - 1 = 2(b+1+d)b - 1 = 2b² + 2b(1+d) - 1.\n\nSo a² + b² = 2ab - 1 + (1+d)² + 1 = (2ab-1) + (1+d)² + 1.\n\nHmm, let me redo: a² + b² = 2b² + 2b(1+d) + (1+d)². And 2ab - 1 = 2b² + 2b(1+d) - 1. So a² + b² = (2ab-1) + (1+d)² + 1 = (2ab-1) + d² + 2d + 2.\n\nSince d | (a²+b²) and a²+b² = 20(2ab-1)/19, we need d | 20(2ab-1)/19.\n\nAlso, 2ab - 1 = 2b² + 2b(1+d) - 1. Modulo d: 2ab - 1 ≡ 2b² + 2b - 1 (mod d). And a² + b² ≡ 2b² + 2b + 1 (mod d) (setting d=0, so a = b+1, a²+b² = (b+1)²+b² = 2b²+2b+1).\n\nSo d | (2b² + 2b + 1). And also from the ratio condition: 19(2b²+2b+1) ≡ 19(a²+b²) = 20(2ab-1) ≡ 20(2b²+2b-1) (mod d).\n\nSo 19(2b²+2b+1) ≡ 20(2b²+2b-1) (mod d).\n19(2b²+2b+1) - 20(2b²+2b-1) ≡ 0 (mod d).\n(38b²+38b+19) - (40b²+40b-20) ≡ 0 (mod d).\n-2b² - 2b + 39 ≡ 0 (mod d).\nSo d | (2b² + 2b - 39).\n\nBut also d | (2b² + 2b + 1). So d | ((2b²+2b+1) - (2b²+2b-39)) = 40.\n\nSo d | 40! That's a key constraint.\n\nSo a - b - 1 divides 40. The divisors of 40 are: ±1, ±2, ±4, ±5, ±8, ±10, ±20, ±40.\n\nThis is a huge constraint. Now for each possible value of d, we can solve.\n\nGiven d = a - b - 1, so a = b + 1 + d. Substituting into 19a² - 40ab + 19b² + 20 = 0:\n\n19(b+1+d)² - 40(b+1+d)b + 19b² + 20 = 0\n19(b² + 2b(1+d) + (1+d)²) - 40b² - 40b(1+d) + 19b² + 20 = 0\n19b² + 38b(1+d) + 19(1+d)² - 40b² - 40b(1+d) + 19b² + 20 = 0\n(19 - 40 + 19)b² + (38 - 40)b(1+d) + 19(1+d)² + 20 = 0\n-2b² - 2b(1+d) + 19(1+d)² + 20 = 0\n2b² + 2b(1+d) = 19(1+d)² + 20\n2b² + 2(1+d)b - 19(1+d)² - 20 = 0\n\nLet me set t = 1 + d. Then:\n2b² + 2tb - 19t² - 20 = 0\nb = (-2t ± √(4t² + 8(19t² + 20))) / 4\n= (-2t ± √(4t² + 152t² + 160)) / 4\n= (-2t ± √(156t² + 160)) / 4\n= (-2t ± 2√(39t² + 40)) / 4\n= (-t ± √(39t² + 40)) / 2\n\nSo we need 39t² + 40 to be a perfect square, say m². And b = (-t ± m)/2 must be integer.\n\nd | 40, so d ∈ {±1, ±2, ±4, ±5, ±8, ±10, ±20, ±40}, and t = 1 + d.\n\nLet me enumerate:\n\nd = 1, t = 2: 39·4 + 40 = 196 = 14². m = 14. b = (-2 ± 14)/2 = 6 or -8.\nb = 6: a = 6 + 1 + 1 = 8. → (8, 6). ✓ (already found)\nb = -8: a = -8 + 2 = -6. → (-6, -8). ✓ (already found)\n\nd = -1, t = 0: 39·0 + 40 = 40. Not a perfect square.\n\nd = 2, t = 3: 39·9 + 40 = 391. √391 ≈ 19.77. Not perfect square.\n\nd = -2, t = -1: 39·1 + 40 = 79. Not perfect square.\n\nd = 4, t = 5: 39·25 + 40 = 1015. √1015 ≈ 31.86. Not perfect square.\n\nd = -4, t = -3: 39·9 + 40 = 391. Not perfect square.\n\nd = 5, t = 6: 39·36 + 40 = 1444 = 38². m = 38. b = (-6 ± 38)/2 = 16 or -22.\nb = 16: a = 16 + 6 = 22. → (22, 16). ✓\nb = -22: a = -22 + 6 = -16. → (-16, -22). ✓\n\nd = -5, t = -4: 39·16 + 40 = 664. √664 ≈ 25.77. Not perfect square.\n\nd = 8, t = 9: 39·81 + 40 = 3199. √3199 ≈ 56.56. Not perfect square.\n\nd = -8, t = -7: 39·49 + 40 = 1951. √1951 ≈ 44.17. Not perfect square.\n\nd = 10, t = 11: 39·121 + 40 = 4759. √4759 ≈ 68.98. Not perfect square.\n\nd = -10, t = -9: 39·81 + 40 = 3199. Not perfect square.\n\nd = 20, t = 21: 39·441 + 40 = 17239. √17239 ≈ 131.3. 131²=17161, 132²=17424. Not perfect square.\n\nd = -20, t = -19: 39·361 + 40 = 14119. √14119 ≈ 118.8. 118²=13924, 119²=14161. Not perfect square.\n\nd = 40, t = 41: 39·1681 + 40 = 65599. √65599 ≈ 256.1. 256²=65536, 257²=66049. Not perfect square.\n\nd = -40, t = -39: 39·1521 + 40 = 59359. √59359 ≈ 243.6. 243²=59049, 244²=59536. Not perfect square.\n\nSo the only values of d that work are d = 1 and d = 5, giving us exactly four solutions:\n(8, 6), (-6, -8), (22, 16), (-16, -22)\n\nLet me verify all four:\n\n(8, 6): a²+b² = 100, 2ab-1 = 95, 100/95 = 20/19 ✓. a-b-1 = 1, 1|100 ✓.\n(-6, -8): a²+b² = 100, 2ab-1 = 95, 100/95 = 20/19 ✓. a-b-1 = 1, 1|100 ✓.\n(22, 16): a²+b² = 740, 2ab-1 = 703, 740/703 = 20/19 ✓. a-b-1 = 5, 5|740 = 148 ✓.\n(-16, -22): a²+b² = 740, 2ab-1 = 703, 740/703 = 20/19 ✓. a-b-1 = 5, 5|740 ✓.\n\nSum of |a| + |b|:\n(8,6): 8+6 = 14\n(-6,-8): 6+8 = 14\n(22,16): 22+16 = 38\n(-16,-22): 16+22 = 38\n\nTotal = 14 + 14 + 38 + 38 = 104.\n\nThe answer is 104.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786637673}
